.nh
.TH "PB-SFTP" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-sftp - Run sftp with Paperboat machine resolution


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb sftp <standard sftp arguments...> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Run the system sftp with Paperboat machine names. Every argument is passed to sftp
unchanged; pb parses no flags of its own. The destination is the first argument that is not an
option (after -- if present), written [user@]machine with an optional :path, and it is replaced
with the machine's managed SSH address. Host identity checks stay on.

.PP
This command does not support --json output; it rejects that mode before execution. Use --help --json for structured command help.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for sftp


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb sftp homelab
  pb sftp deploy@homelab:/srv/app
  pb sftp -P 2222 homelab
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb(1)\fP
